File a vulnerability report for the validated calendar OAuth state-binding weakness in `/workspace/CampusOne`. Root cause: `services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py` creates `CalendarOAuthState` with `user` at start, but `CalendarOAuthCallbackView` (`AllowAny`) later resolves state only by opaque `state` + `used_at__isnull=True`, exchanges the provider `code`, and updates/creates `CalendarIntegrationConnection` for `state.institute` without authenticating the callback caller or verifying `request.user` matches `CalendarOAuthState.user`. This enables a different browser session or unauthenticated actor who knows a live `state` value to complete the provider OAuth flow with their own provider account and bind it to the victim institute/account context. Prioritize the demonstrated impact of cross-session callback completion; also mention the replay/race window because `used_at` is set only after exchange/update/create/sync. Use these exact code locations in the report: `services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py:91`, `services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py:98`, `services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py:106`, `services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py:107`, `services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py:110`, `services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py:114`, `services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py:116`, `services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py:126`, `services/api/modules/school_calendar/models.py:69`, and related connection uniqueness in `services/api/modules/school_calendar/models.py:45`. Evidence available from discovery review:
- callback code snippet resolves `state` only by opaque value and unused flag;
- callback has `AllowAny` and no `request.user` or `CalendarOAuthState.user` comparison;
- start view records initiating user in state but callback ignores it.
If needed, derive the fix inline: require authenticated callback completion bound to the initiating user/session, or store/verify a signed nonce tied to the authenticated user and mark state used atomically before token exchange. Apply/report only if you are fully satisfied the issue is real and dedupe-safe.
